    "title": "Malvern Gene Company to Raise $115M from Convertible Notes While Dealing with Stock Decline - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Leah Mikulich ,\n15 hours ago Ocugen CEO Shankar Musunuri. The company plans to raise $115 million from convertible notes in order to pay debts and keep cash flowing through 2028. Malvern-based Ocugen saw its stock fall almost 20 percent after an announcement to use convertible notes to pay down existing debt and fund ongoing drug development, writes John George for the Philadelphia Business Journal. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
